  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule now exist, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data exploration.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` view (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`) has time field `timestamp`, plus `clientip`, `bytes`, `response` and `response.keyword`, `url.keyword`, `geo.*`, `agent`, `machine.os`, and `extension`. `response` is a string field, so I used `response.keyword` for exact codes.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-b74b8e72 Web logs overview`** (id `eff-b74b8e72-web-logs-overview-192f12d51f87`), default time range last 1 year:\n- Total requests (count), metric\n- Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`), metric\n- Average response size in bytes, metric\n- Requests over time, line chart by `timestamp` date histogram\n- Requests by response code, bar chart on `response.keyword`\n- Top requested URLs, table on `url.keyword`\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-b74b8e72 5xx spike`** (id `c4731f1e-6142-4f2e-9ac5-94501cccdb99`), type `.es-query`, runs every 1m, fires when the count is greater than 10 over a 5-minute window. The query matches `response.keyword` between \"500\" and \"599\". I also tagged it `EFF-b74b8e72`. The status is `pending` because it has only just started.\n\nChoices I made that you may want to change:\n- The 5xx match uses a string range, which is correct for three-digit codes but would be wrong for any non-standard code.\n- The time range is last 1 year, because I couldn't confirm the sample data's date span. I didn't check whether the data falls inside that window.\n- I didn't verify the data's contents directly. `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` isn't set in my shell, so I relied on the MCP tools. The dashboard panels will show the actual response codes and values.",
